{
  "_doc": "map-manifest (FR-MAP-4; SPECIFICATIONS section 6.10, SD-49; design rule D7): the committed size, SHA-256 and bounding box of the 3 per-branch PMTiles files, the baked track set (with its turn-by-turn steps, P6-ROUTE-BAKE) and the routing files of the same OSRM run (kind routing, ohio.osrm.*, read only by the routing service). The files are release downloads, never git. `pnpm run setup:maps` downloads each into .build/data/maps (or $MAPS_DIR) and checks it (--no-routing leaves the routing files out); setup stops with MAP_HASH_MISMATCH <file> on a difference (a routing file only when present); a file over sizeGateBytes (2 GiB per file, C6, owner ruling be2d3f8a) fails. Rewrite after an intended re-bake with: node packages/maps/src/cli.ts write-manifest --dir <dir> --tag <new release tag>. The map files are the Protomaps build 20260811 cut by infra/data/maps/run.sh (release maps-data-v1); the routing files are its OSRM 26.10.0 run of Nov 10, 2026 (first released as maps-data-v2); the tracks are the legs of the F-292 seeded schedule routed on those same routing files on Nov 14, 2026, released together with byte-identical copies of them as maps-data-v3 (OSRM partition output is not byte-reproducible, so the routing files were not re-cut); boxes: infra/data/s8/boxes.json.",
